### Stage 6 — Repair Management Finance API
### Environment: Spring Boot 8081 / MySQL 3306.
### IntelliJ HTTP Client. Replace IDs and credentials with your own.
@base = http://localhost:8081
@companyId = 1
@orderId = 1
@repairId = 1
@invoiceId = 1
@feeId = 1
@managerEmail = owner@example.com
@managerPassword = DemoPassword123!
@customerEmail = customer@example.com
@customerPassword = DemoPassword123!
@platformEmail = platform-admin@example.com
@platformPassword = AdminPassword123!

### 1. Create DRAFT invoice for a COMPLETED order (manager/owner)
POST {{base}}/api/companies/{{companyId}}/invoices
Authorization: Basic {{managerEmail}} {{managerPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": {{orderId}}, "taxAmount": 0.00}

### Alternative: invoice for a COMPLETED/DELIVERED repair
POST {{base}}/api/companies/{{companyId}}/invoices
Authorization: Basic {{managerEmail}} {{managerPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"repairId": {{repairId}}, "taxAmount": 0.00}

### 2. Issue the invoice (UTC date/time in the future)
POST {{base}}/api/companies/{{companyId}}/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/issue
Authorization: Basic {{managerEmail}} {{managerPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"dueAt": "2027-12-31T00:00:00"}

### 3. View issued invoice as customer (only own invoice)
GET {{base}}/api/companies/{{companyId}}/invoices/{{invoiceId}}
Authorization: Basic {{customerEmail}} {{customerPassword}}

### 4. Record money already received — manual operation, NOT a payment gateway.
### Use your actual receipt/bank reference. Do NOT record until the payment is verified.
POST {{base}}/api/companies/{{companyId}}/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/payments
Authorization: Basic {{managerEmail}} {{managerPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount": 80.00, "method": "BANK_TRANSFER", "reference": "BANK-TRANSFER-2026-001"}

### 5. Expense (company-level)
POST {{base}}/api/companies/{{companyId}}/expenses
Authorization: Basic {{managerEmail}} {{managerPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"category": "RENT", "description": "Monthly workshop rent", "amount": 200.00, "expenseDate": "2026-10-22"}

### 6. Company Finance Dashboard
GET {{base}}/api/companies/{{companyId}}/finance/overview
Authorization: Basic {{managerEmail}} {{managerPassword}}

### 7. Platform fee (SUPER_ADMIN only). Created as PENDING, not yet earned.
POST {{base}}/api/platform/finance/fees
Authorization: Basic {{platformEmail}} {{platformPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"companyId": {{companyId}}, "orderId": {{orderId}}, "feeType": "COMMISSION", "amount": 4.00}

### 8. Mark fee earned — manual recognition, NOT a payment capture.
POST {{base}}/api/platform/finance/fees/{{feeId}}/earn
Authorization: Basic {{platformEmail}} {{platformPassword}}

### 9. Platform operating expense (SUPER_ADMIN only)
POST {{base}}/api/platform/finance/expenses
Authorization: Basic {{platformEmail}} {{platformPassword}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"category": "HOSTING", "description": "Monthly VPS", "amount": 25.00, "currencyCode": "EUR", "expenseDate": "2026-10-22"}

### 10. Platform Finance dashboard — separately aggregated by currency.
GET {{base}}/api/platform/finance/overview
Authorization: Basic {{platformEmail}} {{platformPassword}}

### Other useful GETs:
### /api/companies/{companyId}/invoices
### /api/companies/{companyId}/invoices/mine
### /api/companies/{companyId}/expenses
### /api/companies/{companyId}/invoices/{invoiceId}/void (POST)
